      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When standard counters are clean but loss persists, consider looking into Quality of Service (QoS) policy misconfigurations or policing mechanisms on that edge device. An aggressive rate limiter or an improperly configured queue can drop packets only when flow thresholds are momentarily crossed, leading to random-looking loss. Investigating flow statistics or analyzing traffic timestamps around the loss events might help pinpoint the exact moment the sporadic drop occurs.",
